<pending_commit branch="master" change_id="Iefd46f68682852a64d4fb89b49c2279f78659780" commit="5d8913e3e234543bbc7ed20d4ef84e736064ce52" commit_message="offline test: stop when a test item failed, show failed item in log.  Now the offline test will stop when a test item failed. When fetching result, the test will show the name (pytest name or shtest name) of the failed test in error message.  Fix a bug in stressapptest, it used to ignore reboot event.  BUG=chromium:573933 TEST=None  Change-Id: Iefd46f68682852a64d4fb89b49c2279f78659780 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/339515 Commit-Ready: Wei-Han Chen &lt;stimim@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Wei-Han Chen &lt;stimim@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Wei-Han Chen &lt;stimim@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="339515" owner_email="stimim@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="9" project="chromiumos/platform/factory" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/factory" ref="refs/changes/15/339515/9" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I8654bdc74658222a3b4c98f8674c1b3cd2ada42f" commit="201ddb65253b1d1cbfbfc9afeeae99fb7a8f20e8" commit_message="offline-test: fetch_log: fix typo  fix a typo in fetch_log.py  BUG=None TEST=manually  Change-Id: I8654bdc74658222a3b4c98f8674c1b3cd2ada42f Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/340940 Commit-Ready: Wei-Han Chen &lt;stimim@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Wei-Han Chen &lt;stimim@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Shun-Hsing Ou &lt;shunhsingou@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="1" gerrit_number="340940" owner_email="stimim@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="8" project="chromiumos/platform/factory" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/factory" ref="refs/changes/40/340940/8" remote="cros" total_fail_count="1"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I4cc7eba2fa99e282acdeafc9652bafde566195e2" commit="f86048b198b5272478d6f6a9be41d5e382f28648" commit_message="offline test: sync file system  Some device will directly reboot even if we use 'shutdown -h now', for those devices, to make sure offline test starts on the right time, we will not shutdown or reboot the device, but ask operator to unplug the device directly. In this case, we have to sync the file system to prevent from any data loss.  We also add &quot;sync&quot; command on &quot;die&quot; (test failed) and &quot;all_test_passed&quot; in main.sh.  BUG=chromium:573933 TEST=manual test  Change-Id: I4cc7eba2fa99e282acdeafc9652bafde566195e2 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/340923 Commit-Ready: Wei-Han Chen &lt;stimim@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Wei-Han Chen &lt;stimim@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Shun-Hsing Ou &lt;shunhsingou@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="1" gerrit_number="340923" owner_email="stimim@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="7" project="chromiumos/platform/factory" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/factory" ref="refs/changes/23/340923/7" remote="cros" total_fail_count="1"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I15d7d3f4d2d9a5307a6a625fef01b283c5894907" commit="2587d5f30325ca5458b690c484a7770ea7ce5d6f" commit_message="log_writer: fix seq file write speed  GlobalSeq was calling fsync on the seq file after every increment, resulting in testThreadsWithoutSleep failing on a co-worker's machine.  He was getting 120~130 writes per second (non-SSD), whereas I was getting around 2000 (SSD).  Since we increase the sequence number by SEQ_INCREMENT_ON_BOOT every reboot, we can remove the fsync call and retain the monotonicity property, optimizing for speed.  This may be important in cases where Goofy rapidly outputs a large volume of log messages to disk.  Now testThreadsWithoutSleep is getting around 6000 writes on co-worker's machine (non-SSD), and 10000 writes on my machine (SSD).  BUG=chromium:609069 TEST=Manually on local machine  Change-Id: I15d7d3f4d2d9a5307a6a625fef01b283c5894907 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/342807 Commit-Ready: Joel Kitching &lt;kitching@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Joel Kitching &lt;kitching@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Wei-Han Chen &lt;stimim@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="342807" owner_email="kitching@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="2" project="chromiumos/platform/factory" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/factory" ref="refs/changes/07/342807/2" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="Idd9038493a7d13101d33eb01a0a98b2c84a1d17c" commit="ab7ab8cf8dabf079306821664796628f01c8d884" commit_message="oak: update dark resume wakeup source  IRQ wakeup is now implemented in mwifiex driver instead of a separate mwifiex platform driver. Update dark resume source to match the changes.  BUG=chrome-os-partner:47791 TEST=`test_that -b oak DUT network_WiFi_WoWLAN` passes  Change-Id: Idd9038493a7d13101d33eb01a0a98b2c84a1d17c Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/333200 Commit-Ready: Wei-Ning Huang &lt;wnhuang@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Wei-Ning Huang &lt;wnhuang@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Wei-Ning Huang &lt;wnhuang@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="333200" owner_email="wnhuang@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="4" project="chromiumos/overlays/board-overlays" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/overlays/board-overlays" ref="refs/changes/00/333200/4" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="Id85c60b2d4a4ff811f87bc83136aabfd4ffdcc57" commit="b76a0eadeca6deaf8bc97d41ee72365516f77457" commit_message="thermal_load: change loop condition  ADBlink runs significantly longer then local link. Old code which runs a fixed loop count will not terminate in expected time, we need to measure the elapsed time for a precise terminate condition.  BUG=chrome-os-partner:53061 TEST=Run thermal_load test  Change-Id: Id85c60b2d4a4ff811f87bc83136aabfd4ffdcc57 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/342836 Commit-Ready: Ting Shen &lt;phoenixshen@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Ting Shen &lt;phoenixshen@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Wei-Han Chen &lt;stimim@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="342836" owner_email="phoenixshen@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="2" project="chromiumos/platform/factory" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/factory" ref="refs/changes/36/342836/2" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I1f42cd245c245ab4f90c66671e6249bbb333680f" commit="380244a3008072c68313762ea0166f96daf6a4bc" commit_message="elm: Add DRM HDMI driver load udev rule and script into rootfs  When DRM HDMI driver is loaded, the DRM emits a udev event. This udev event triggers the new rule &quot;99-mtk_drm_hdmi_load.rules&quot; added by this patch, which causes the script &quot;hdcp_pass_key.sh&quot; to run.  The script &quot;hdcp_pass_key.sh&quot; will then get the HDCP key and pass this key to HDCP driver.  BUG=chrome-os-partner:50899 TEST=test HDCP can be successfully enabled  Change-Id: I1f42cd245c245ab4f90c66671e6249bbb333680f Signed-off-by: Cawa Cheng &lt;cawa.cheng@mediatek.com&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/341335 Commit-Ready: Daniel Kurtz &lt;djkurtz@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: cawa cheng &lt;cawa.cheng@mediatek.com&gt; Reviewed-by: Daniel Kurtz &lt;djkurtz@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Nicolas Boichat &lt;drinkcat@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="341335" owner_email="cawa.cheng@mediatek.com" pass_count="0" patch_number="12" project="chromiumos/overlays/board-overlays" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/overlays/board-overlays" ref="refs/changes/35/341335/12" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I29c10817cf71ae51d12092f05228e92f342ca4e5" commit="30fa071292ef2017b13e3f6ef9f2b934586962ab" commit_message="minigbm: remove GBM_BO_USE_WRITE from the drivers.  We deprecated GBM_BO_USE_WRITE in Chrome OS, so we should remove it from the drivers.  BUG=chromium:356871 CQ-DEPEND=CL:342391 Change-Id: I29c10817cf71ae51d12092f05228e92f342ca4e5 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/341911 Commit-Ready: Dongseong Hwang &lt;dongseong.hwang@intel.com&gt; Tested-by: Dongseong Hwang &lt;dongseong.hwang@intel.com&gt; Reviewed-by: Dongseong Hwang &lt;dongseong.hwang@intel.com&gt; Reviewed-by: Zach Reizner &lt;zachr@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="2" gerrit_number="341911" owner_email="dongseong.hwang@intel.com" pass_count="0" patch_number="6" project="chromiumos/platform/minigbm" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/minigbm" ref="refs/changes/11/341911/6" remote="cros" total_fail_count="4"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-3.18" change_id="I5a4570b17d106881f19f119e427fce7aa20091f0" commit="781269a6499ae39ed14100ba166824be93545afb" commit_message="CHROMIUM: drm/mediatek: remove suspend/resume in dsi  The DSI encoder doesn't need its suspend/resume callbacks since those just enable/disable the DSI encoder. This is taken care of by enabling and disabling the display. It also causes problems when the display is left off during suspend, so just remove the callbacks.  BUG=chrome-os-partner:52916 TEST=power_Resume on oak  Change-Id: I5a4570b17d106881f19f119e427fce7aa20091f0 Signed-off-by: Derek Basehore &lt;dbasehore@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/342845 Commit-Ready: Daniel Kurtz &lt;djkurtz@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Daniel Kurtz &lt;djkurtz@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="342845" owner_email="dbasehore@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/45/342845/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I5c599489c97655317d42022c2ebbebeb91110a38" commit="74aa7957bd43fad4a7dcc58e629adf8780eb2ca8" commit_message="Add test for simple value check.  There are many tests that requires reading a value and checking with a given expected value. Provide a test for doing this kind of check.  BUG=None TEST=Manually on Lucid  Change-Id: I5c599489c97655317d42022c2ebbebeb91110a38 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/342793 Commit-Ready: Shun-Hsing Ou &lt;shunhsingou@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Shun-Hsing Ou &lt;shunhsingou@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Ting Shen &lt;phoenixshen@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="342793" owner_email="shunhsingou@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="2" project="chromiumos/platform/factory" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/factory" ref="refs/changes/93/342793/2" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-3.18" change_id="I782e0a4501e81ba2c9925a2c9571333655cd6845" commit="edd98cc3908da81b49d86aa032381bd8a2932c56" commit_message="FROMLIST: mmc: mmc: Fix partition switch timeout for some eMMCs  Some eMMCs set the partition switch timeout too low.  Now typically eMMCs are considered a critical component (e.g. because they store the root file system) and consequently are expected to be reliable.  Thus we can neglect the use case where eMMCs can't switch reliably and we might want a lower timeout to facilitate speedy recovery.  Although we could employ a quirk for the cards that are affected (if we could identify them all), as described above, there is little benefit to having a low timeout, so instead simply set a minimum timeout.  The minimum is set to 300ms somewhat arbitrarily - the examples that have been seen had a timeout of 10ms but were sometimes taking 60-70ms.  (from http://thread.gmane.org/gmane.linux.kernel.mmc/37402)  Signed-off-by: Adrian Hunter &lt;adrian.hunter@intel.com&gt;  BUG=chrome-os-partner:52781 TEST=run BootDevice and ConsecutiveBoot with 5000 test cycles without eMMC errors and test works correctly.  Change-Id: I782e0a4501e81ba2c9925a2c9571333655cd6845 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/342161 Commit-Ready: Wenkai Du &lt;wenkai.du@intel.com&gt; Tested-by: Wenkai Du &lt;wenkai.du@intel.com&gt; Reviewed-by: Gwendal Grignou &lt;gwendal@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Benson Leung &lt;bleung@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="342161" owner_email="wenkai.du@intel.com" pass_count="0" patch_number="4" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/61/342161/4" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><lkgm version="8287.0.0-rc2"/></manifest>